  "vibe": "Plum-velvet room (#2a1420) with brass (#cf9b52) catching the light, cream (#f0e8da) type and a teal stage wash (#34687a) as the second chip. Yeseva One's high-contrast decorative serif over geometric Jost. The world is a basement jazz club: a brass-tinted spotlight triangle sweeping side to side on a 0.6Hz sine with its elliptical pool of light tracking underneath, four cream musical notes rising and fading on a slow 0.16Hz cycle, and along the whole bottom edge a fourteen-key piano keyboard where one white key lights up at a time on a marching index, black keys laid over it. Its signature mechanic is the front-of-house slider — a pointer dragging a level to a big percentage, then flipping a switch. Brass-glow feature cards, drowse titles, calm 0.5-roll camera. For live venues, bars, festivals and any brand that trades in evenings.",
